    <footnotes>
        <footnote id="F1">Each restricted stock unit (&quot;RSU&quot;) relates to one share of common stock, par value $0.001 per share (&quot;Common Stock&quot;), of Silvia, Inc. (formerly known as ProCap Financial, Inc.) (the &quot;Issuer&quot;). Vested RSUs will be settled in accordance with the ProCap Financial, Inc. 2025 Equity Incentive Plan (the &quot;Plan&quot;) and the applicable award agreement.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F2">The RSUs vest in tranches if the closing price of the Common Stock meets or exceeds the applicable stock price target for five continuous business days, subject to the Reporting Person's continued employment through the date the applicable target is achieved, as follows: 250,000 RSUs at each of $15.00, $17.50, $20.00, $22.50 and $25.00; 500,000 RSUs at each of $27.50, $30.00, $32.50, $35.00 and $37.50; 750,000 RSUs at each of $40.00, $42.50 and $45.00; and 1,000,000 RSUs at each of $47.50 and $50.00.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F3">RSUs that have not vested will be forfeited without consideration upon the earlier of (a) the seventh anniversary of December 5, 2025 and (b) the termination of the Reporting Person's employment for any reason. The number of RSUs and the stock price targets are subject to equitable adjustment by the Issuer's Board of Directors in connection with the capital changes specified in the Reporting Person's employment agreement and as provided in the Plan.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F4">Through administrative oversight, the RSUs, were not reported on the Reporting Person's original Form 4 filed on December 9, 2025.</footnote>
